I've got an aureal vortext II card (au8830), and while the alsa driver
(versions 1.01, 1.02c and 1.03) produce sound, it seems to get random
distortions.  There are times when a rapid succession of short sounds (eg
AIM sounds) when the sounds will speed up, slow down,  become aliased, or
become staticy.   I've also noticed recently that while listening to
longer sounds (eg music) that the music will sometimes switch sides
intermitantly.  I didn't notice this before probably because I just
started using head phones more often than the speakers.  I'm using Debian
Woody 3.0r2, kernel 2.4.25 with alsadriver 1.03 downloaded and compiled
with gcc 2.95.4.  I'm not sure what other info would be useful for
troubleshooting, but let me know and I'll see what I can do to provide it.
--Greg



